# TDD Workflow

> Load this when implementing features, fixing bugs, or refactoring.
> These rules are MANDATORY for this user.

---

## 🔴 TDD: RED → GREEN → REFACTOR

**Always write the test first. Always.**

```
🔴 RED    → Write failing test
🟢 GREEN  → Minimal code to pass
🔵 REFACTOR → Improve while staying green
```

### Applies to EVERYTHING

- New features
- Bug fixes
- Refactoring
- Entities, UseCases, Services, Repositories, Controllers

### Workflow

**RED — Write test first:**

```java
// GetUserServiceTest.java
@Test
@DisplayName("Should throw when User not found")
void shouldThrowWhenUserNotFound() {
    when(repository.findById(1L)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());

    assertThrows(UserNotFoundException.class, () -> service.getUserById(1L));
}
// Run: mvn test -Dtest=GetUserServiceTest → MUST FAIL
```

**GREEN — Minimal implementation:**

```java
// GetUserService.java
@Override
public User getUserById(Long userId) {
    return repository.findById(userId)
            .orElseThrow(UserNotFoundException::new);
}
// Run: mvn test -Dtest=GetUserServiceTest → MUST PASS
```

**REFACTOR — Improve with confidence:**

```java
@Override
public User getUserById(Long userId) {
    logger.info("GET USER SERVICE - GET USER BY ID - User ID: {}", userId);

    return repository.findById(userId)
            .orElseThrow(UserNotFoundException::new);
}
// Run: mvn test -Dtest=GetUserServiceTest → STILL PASSES
```

### Bug Fix Pattern

```java
// 1. Write test that reproduces the bug (RED)
@Test
@DisplayName("Should reject CPF that already exists on registry")
void shouldRejectCpfThatAlreadyExists() {
    when(repository.findByCpf(EXISTING_CPF)).thenReturn(Optional.of(existingUser));

    assertThrows(InvalidUserException.class, () -> service.registry(newUserWithSameCpf));
}
// Run → FAIL (confirms bug exists)

// 2. Fix the code (GREEN)
// 3. Run test → PASS (confirms fix)
// 4. Refactor if needed
```

### Anti-patterns

```java
// ❌ Code before test
// ❌ Skip RED (if test passes immediately, you're not testing the right thing)
// ❌ Refactor without green tests
// ❌ Fix bug without a reproducing test
```

---

## 🎯 Feature is DONE When

```
Unit tests (domain.service) ✅ + Integration tests (application.controller / infrastructure.repository) ✅ = DONE
```

## 🧱 TDD por Camada (Clean Architecture)

- **domain** (`Service`/UseCase): teste puro com Mockito — mock apenas o `Repository` (interface), sem contexto Spring (`@SpringBootTest`).
- **application** (`Controller`): `@WebMvcTest` + `MockMvc`, com o `Service`/UseCase mockado via `@MockBean`.
- **infrastructure** (`Repository`): `@DataJpaTest` (H2) ou teste de integração validando o mapeamento `Model` ↔ `Domain` contra um banco real.
- **application.validation**: teste unitário direto do `ConstraintValidator` (sem subir contexto Spring), cobrindo valor válido/inválido/nulo.

